        "label": "What's Going On With the Raptors",
        "body": "The Toronto Raptors' offseason isn't whispering - it's building, and the loudest move came just yesterday. <strong>Toronto has signed Jaden Bradley, their 50th-draft pick out of Arizona, to a two-way contract</strong>, injecting Big 12 defensive grit and 39.4% three-point shooting into the roster's future. After a season that ended at 46-36 and a third-place Atlantic finish, the front office is clearly pivoting toward depth and versatility rather than chasing a quick fix. Bradley, the Big 12 Player of the Year and third-team All-American, arrives with a proven track record of 13.3 points and 4.4 assists per game last season - numbers that could translate quickly in the G League or as a backup guard. With Leonard now in Toronto and Quickley finally free to play his style, the team's identity is sharpening. <strong>What to watch in camp: whether Bradley earns a rotation spot and how quickly the two-way slots fill with Alijah Martin and Chucky Hepburn</strong>.",
